Subject: [PATCH] feat(language): the owner's own request for a language wins
 (D752)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The founder, 9 Oct: „Users request toward their assistant always wins."
Nothing remembered such a request: „მომწერე ინგლისურად" is written in
Georgian, so the next reply read the line as Georgian and the request lost.
A request in the owner's own line (ka / en / ru / es, a verb of writing or
speaking plus a language) is stored as reply_language and read before the
conversation, the number and the name — in the owner's run, userLanguage
and threadLanguage — until they ask for another. One line naming two
languages is not read as a request.

Unit tests, and a real-Postgres test of the threads ↔ user_profile_kv join
(integer vs text, the 2080 pair) through scripts/ops/malformed.sh.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
